Q1: NULL handling: AND sla_status IS NOT NULL at handler.py:35. NULLs invisible to both counts.
Q2: Only "Overdue" as failure? Yes — single comparison in the entire handler. "At Risk" if it appeared would count as met.
Q3: Normalization? None. Zero occurrences of strip/lower/upper in the handler.
Q4: Zero valid jobs? Returns sla_compliance = None, writes NULL to DB, returns "sla_compliance_pct": None in response. No error raised.
Q5: Rounding — DB vs response?
DB write (handler.py:58): raw float stored unrounded
Response (handler.py:64): round(sla_compliance, 2)
