PART 4 — DELETE+INSERT pattern
Q1: Exact code (handler.py:52-59):
cur.execute("DELETE FROM sla_tracker_output WHERE vendor_id = %s", (vendor_id,))
cur.execute(
    "INSERT INTO sla_tracker_output (vendor_id, avg_response_time, avg_completion_time, sla_compliance) VALUES (%s,%s,%s,%s)",
    (vendor_id, avg_response_time, avg_completion_time, sla_compliance),
)
conn.commit()
Plain DELETE then INSERT. Not an UPSERT (ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE).
Q2: History preserved? No. No audit table, no history table. Previous record unconditionally deleted. Confirmed — only two references to sla_tracker_output in all Python files, both in this handler.
Q3: vendor_id UNIQUE in sla_tracker_output? Yes — init_db.py:166: vendor_id TEXT UNIQUE.
Q4: Rollback on exception? No except block and no conn.rollback() anywhere in compute_sla_compliance. Structure is try: ... finally: conn.close(). Rollback is implicit only (PostgreSQL rolls back uncommitted transaction when connection closes). Explicit conn.rollback() exists in other handlers (vendor_capacity_mcp, vendor_qualification_mcp) but not here.
Q5: Check for unchanged values before write? None. Always deletes and inserts regardless.
Q6: Full schema of sla_tracker_output (init_db.py:164-170):
id SERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
vendor_id TEXT UNIQUE,
avg_response_time TEXT,
avg_completion_time TEXT,
sla_compliance REAL
5 columns only. No calculation_timestamp, no total_jobs, no sla_met_jobs, no overdue_jobs.
PART 5 — Misc
Q1: Explicit rollback()? No — not in this handler. finally: conn.close() only.
Q2: sla_compliance column type? REAL (init_db.py:169).
Q3: DISTINCT/dedup on vendor_jobs_input? No. No DISTINCT, no dedup. vendor_jobs_input has only id SERIAL PRIMARY KEY — no UNIQUE constraint on (vendor_id, claim_id) or any other combination. Duplicate rows would inflate both numerator and denominator equally (so compliance % stays unchanged), but total_jobs count would be wrong.
Q4: Equal weighting? Yes — sum(1 for ...) counts every row as 1. vendor_jobs_input has no weight, priority, or severity column.
Q5: Other writers to sla_tracker_output? None. Exactly 4 references across the entire codebase — DELETE, INSERT, SELECT (read), and CREATE TABLE — all in sla_compliance_mcp/handler.py and common/init_db.py. No other agent touches this table.
